Scope and modifications

The shp_hex_2013 through shp_hex_2027 datasets adapt The Downballot's district
cartograms: version 2.1 for Congress start years 2013-2021, version 3.0 for
2023, version 3.1 for 2025, and version 3.2 for 2027. District identifiers and
attributes are standardized, narrow gaps and invalid geometry are repaired,
and the 2023 cartogram is translated to align with later versions. The same
version 2.1 geometry is reused for 2013-2021, so these maps do not represent
every historical boundary change.

The shp_hex_2005 through shp_hex_2011 datasets reuse a generated 2009 district
cartogram made with Cory McCartan's hexmap package and Jeffrey B. Lewis's
historical district boundaries. State placement and scaling use The
Downballot / Daily Kos Elections state cartogram, with adjustments for the
older apportionment. The result is rescaled and centered to match the extent
of the version 2.1 district cartogram, and geometry gaps are repaired. This
notice covers those Downballot-derived layout inputs; it does not assert
that all inputs to the generated maps share the same license.

The README figures and sticker reference maps visualize these adapted
cartograms. The normal-vote figure adds independently calculated partisan
colors. The hex cartogram in man/figures/logo.png is recolored, cropped, and
combined with a geographic district map. This CC BY 4.0 notice applies to
the Downballot-derived hexmap material, not the Mapbox basemap or other
components of the logo. Presidential election inputs have separate source
and reuse information documented by cd_normal_vote().

Redistribution

Retain the Daniel Donner / The Downballot credit, source and license links,
and an indication of modifications when sharing the licensed map material,
including in figures or the logo. Accompanying credits may be used where
appropriate to the medium. When distributing a map or sticker separately
from the package, include those credits with it. The licensed material is
provided as-is, subject to the warranty disclaimer in CC BY 4.0.
